userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using Chart.js.

CONCEPT: In y = mx + b, the slope m controls a line's steepness and direction while the intercept b sets where it crosses the y-axis, so any line on a graph can be matched to its equation by reading those two numbers off the picture.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): A line is completely determined by two readable numbers — how fast it climbs (m) and where it cuts the y-axis (b) — so matching graphs to equations is just reading steepness and crossing point off the picture.
DEMO STEPS: 7 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

